# kustomization name -> (area, plain title, one sentence, owner)
#
# owner is a real, required field per layer -- not decoration. Before crew#(this fix), every
# Component/API this file emitted was silently stamped "group:default/platform" from one
# global constant, so via-negativa's Kyverno-catching-a-missing-description gate could never
# have caught a missing OWNER even if it had one to check: there was no per-layer owner to be
# missing. Every row below is explicit now so a new layer must state one instead of silently
# inheriting a default nobody chose (Spotify's own Soundcheck treats exactly this -- "every
# Component has a real owning Group, not a placeholder" -- as a scored, enforced rule, not a
# convention). Real per-team owners are still a follow-up: this repo has no Group entities
# beyond the one default, so "group:default/platform" here is today's honest answer, not a
# forgotten TODO -- render() below refuses a row with no owner at all, same as no description.
